 "kind": "definition",
 "title": "$p$-primary and prime-to-$p$ torsion sheaves",
 "statement": "Let $(C,F)$ be a curve coefficient pair [def-weil-pbc-curve-setting], and let\n$\\operatorname{char}k=p>0$. The sheaf $F$ is *$p$-primary* if every element of\nevery geometric stalk $F_{\\bar c}$ is killed by a power of $p$, and *prime to\n$p$* if every such element has finite order coprime to $p$. In characteristic\nzero, \"prime to the characteristic\" imposes no condition.",
 "source": {
